<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech govt approves plan to raise 1998 energy VAT.</title>
<headline>Czech govt approves plan to raise 1998 energy VAT.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech government approved a plan on Wednesday to raise the value added tax on electricity and natural gas to 22 percent from five percent in 1998, Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus told a news conference.</p>
<p>The hike in the energy VAT, which must still be approved by parliament as do all changes in the tax code, would begin on January 1, 1998, Klaus said.</p>
</text>
